# Netlify custom headers.
#
# Every page on this site requires a signed-in session (checked by
# auth-guard.js's requireAuth()). Without this, clicking the
# browser's Back button after signing out can restore a page straight
# from the browser's back/forward cache (bfcache) — a snapshot of the
# already-rendered DOM from before sign-out — without re-running any
# JS, so it briefly (or indefinitely, on some browsers) shows the
# signed-in page again even though the session is gone.
#
# Cache-Control: no-store tells the browser not to bfcache these
# responses at all, so Back always forces a real navigation, which
# re-runs requireAuth() and redirects to /login exactly like a fresh
# visit would. auth-guard.js also force-reloads on a restored bfcache
# page as a second layer, in case a browser bfcaches anyway.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
